WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.284 --> 00:00:02.127
- Is Canadian a language?

00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:06.707
- I dated a girl from Montreal
for a year and a half.

00:00:06.707 --> 00:00:08.132
I love Canada.

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:09.960
- All right! I've been there twice.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.628
- [Voiceover] What is
the capital of Canada?

00:00:11.628 --> 00:00:13.151
(laughing)

00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:16.341
- I only know, like,
three cities in Canada,

00:00:16.341 --> 00:00:17.926
so I'm just going to say them.

00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:19.428
Montreal...

00:00:20.335 --> 00:00:21.471
what's the other one?

00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:23.857
- Canada's capital?

00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:29.111
Ontario is a whole place...

00:00:29.111 --> 00:00:32.360
- The capital, the capital of Canada?

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.552
- Let's go with Toronto,
where my Blue Jays at!

00:00:35.552 --> 00:00:38.780
- It's either Toronto, Quebec,

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.708
or there's something with Victoria in it.

00:00:43.285 --> 00:00:44.752
- Ottawa is a city?

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:47.005
- [Voiceover] Who is
the president of Canada?

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:50.125
(laughing)

00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:53.503
- I don't think I've ever heard
of the president of Canada.

00:00:53.503 --> 00:00:54.812
- Poutine.

00:00:54.812 --> 00:00:56.840
- I bet he's bald.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.632
Or like a stern lady.

00:00:58.632 --> 00:00:59.544
- They don't have a president!

00:00:59.544 --> 00:01:01.762
They got a prime minister, right?

00:01:01.762 --> 00:01:03.472
- They got all that French influence.

00:01:03.472 --> 00:01:04.890
Once you get Europe in your system,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.067
all you're going to do
is have prime ministers.

00:01:09.812 --> 00:01:10.979
- [Voiceover] Stephen Harper.

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:12.439
- Stephen Hopper?

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.548
- [Voiceover] Harper.

00:01:13.548 --> 00:01:15.416
- Harper? Stephen Harper?

00:01:15.416 --> 00:01:17.229
Stephen Harper.

00:01:20.952 --> 00:01:24.430
- I was told that there wasn't
going to be math in this.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.383
- A hundred million people.

00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:26.943
- Under a million people.

00:01:26.943 --> 00:01:28.163
- Thirty million?

00:01:28.163 --> 00:01:29.748
- I feel like nobody lives there.

00:01:29.748 --> 00:01:32.967
I feel like I've visited
and seen thirty people.

00:01:37.136 --> 00:01:40.091
- They're a tenth the size of America?

00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:41.677
- Canada's pretty big.

00:01:41.677 --> 00:01:43.220
But just 'cause it's pretty
big, doesn't mean that

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.683
it has people everywhere.

00:01:44.683 --> 00:01:45.931
'Cause it's kinda cold.

00:01:45.931 --> 00:01:47.768
Drake doesn't even live
there, so that says a lot.

00:01:51.127 --> 00:01:51.853
- Ryan Gosling.

00:01:51.853 --> 00:01:52.736
- Ryan Gosling.

00:01:52.736 --> 00:01:53.617
- Ryan Gosling.

00:01:53.617 --> 00:01:54.898
- Ryan Gosling.

00:01:54.898 --> 00:01:56.149
That's the one I knew.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.193
That's the one that I
should have remembered

00:01:58.193 --> 00:02:01.163
because he's, like, perfect.

00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:03.910
Bear.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.742
- What lives in Canada?

00:02:05.742 --> 00:02:06.830
A whale?

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.255
- Badger.

00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:10.846
It's got to be a 'b'.

00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:13.069
- A bear. No, a moose.

00:02:13.593 --> 00:02:15.060
A bear moose.

00:02:16.294 --> 00:02:18.421
- Ah, beaver.

00:02:18.421 --> 00:02:21.808
Yeah, I knew it was a
'b' and it was mammal.

00:02:24.886 --> 00:02:27.319
- It's a red maple leaf.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:29.349
No, it's a white maple leaf on red,

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.776
or is it a red maple leaf on white?

00:02:32.394 --> 00:02:34.371
Oh, I think I'm thinking of Japan.

00:02:34.371 --> 00:02:36.031
I do care about Canada.

00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:37.232
I'm from Wisconsin.

00:02:37.232 --> 00:02:39.693
Although I'm very proud that
Wisconsin doesn't touch Canada.

00:02:39.693 --> 00:02:41.444
People think Wisconsin does touch Canada,

00:02:41.444 --> 00:02:43.447
but Minnesota's our little shield,

00:02:43.447 --> 00:02:47.450
and Michigan's our little hat.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.952
So they don't...

00:02:48.952 --> 00:02:50.759
please don't put this in.

